IMPORT prelude

-- Electoral Act 1907 (Western Australia) -- who is entitled to be enrolled and to vote (s 17), enrolment at 16 and 17 (s 17AA),
-- people not entitled to vote or be enrolled (s 18), and compulsory voting (Part IV Division 7: s 155AB, s 156): the elector's duty,
-- the penalty notice and its modified penalty, the infringement notice, the offence and its fine.
--
-- Edition: compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 47953, retrieved 7 September 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47953.txt. The deposit names no compilation number or compilation date. Its compilation table
-- ends with the Electoral Amendment (Names of Registered Political Parties) Act 2024 (No. 46 of 2024, in force 16 November 2024); the
-- last reprint listed is Reprint 17 as at 9 December 2016.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement au/wa:REQ-0013 (priority 1), raised 3 times by the Western Australian cradle-to-grave lives: Chloe c024
-- (2021-03-13, "the State election, the day before her eighteenth birthday: too young by a day" -- "Who may vote in a State
-- election?", s 17), Chloe c046 (2025-03-08, "First State election" -- "Compulsory?", s 156) and Jake k045 (2029-03-08, "The State
-- election: enrolled by then, does not vote; a fine", s 156). The ledger names "s 156 (compulsory voting); s 17 (entitlement to
-- enrol: 18)". SCOPED to those questions first, with the definitions (s 4: elector, election, Council election; s 16C whole of
-- State electorate; s 155AB), conditions and exceptions needed to answer them.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: administration (Part II), districts and boundaries (Part IIB), the register and rolls beyond the definition of an
-- elector, claims and objections (ss 19-50 and following), ss 17A and 17B (overseas and itinerant electors), s 17(4) (members and
-- spouses), how provisional, postal and early votes are cast, nominations, polling and scrutiny, s 156AA (evidentiary certificates),
-- and everything after s 156. The text is the CURRENT compilation: the 2021 election (c024) was held under an earlier text (ss 17AA
-- and 16C, and amendments to ss 17, 18 and 156, came later, per their history notes) that was not deposited. The "prescribed period"
-- for sending a penalty notice and the amount the Commissioner actually sets as a modified penalty are not in this Act: INPUTS. The
-- Act states only the CAPS ($50, $75) and the fines ($200, $1 000).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions (the skill was not available in this
-- session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Electoral Act 1907 (WA) -- enrolment, the vote and compulsory voting`

§§ `helpers`

-- Dates are given as year, month and day. That a person attains an age at the start of the anniversary of their birth is an
-- INFERENCE (the general rule); the Act does not say.
GIVEN `birth year` IS A NUMBER, `birth month` IS A NUMBER, `birth day` IS A NUMBER, `on year` IS A NUMBER, `on month` IS A NUMBER, `on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`age in completed years` MEANS
    IF `on month` GREATER THAN `birth month` OR (`on month` EQUALS `birth month` AND `on day` AT LEAST `birth day`)
    THEN `on year` MINUS `birth year`
    ELSE `on year` MINUS `birth year` MINUS 1

-- The facts about a person that ss 17, 17AA and 18 ask. Age is passed separately, so that one person can be tested at several ages.
DECLARE Person HAS
    `is an Australian citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a pre-1984 British subject elector` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has lived in the district for at least 1 month` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is enrolled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `continues to live in the district` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the subject of a lack of capacity notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is off the Commonwealth roll under section 93(8)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was convicted of treason and not pardoned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is serving or yet to serve 1 year or longer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a temporary visa or is an unlawful noncitizen` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `18 -- people not entitled to vote and be enrolled`

-- s 18(1): "A person is not entitled to vote in an election if the person -- (a) is the subject of a lack of capacity notice; or (aa)
-- is not on the Commonwealth roll for this State under the ground specified in the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 section 93(8)(a);
-- or (b) has been convicted of treason and has not been granted a pardon ...; or (c) is serving or is yet to serve a sentence of
-- detention (imposed under the Young Offenders Act 1994), or imprisonment, of 1 year or longer; ... or (d) is the holder of a
-- temporary visa ... or is an unlawful noncitizen". (2): "A person mentioned in subsection (1)(a), (aa), (b) or (d) is not entitled to
-- be enrolled as an elector." So a prisoner (c) may stay enrolled but may not vote. Paragraphs (ca)-(cd) (indefinite imprisonment,
-- Criminal Code orders, supervised persons) are folded into nothing here: not encoded.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `barred from enrolment by section 18(2)` IF
        `the person`'s `is the subject of a lack of capacity notice`
    OR  `the person`'s `is off the Commonwealth roll under section 93(8)(a)`
    OR  `the person`'s `was convicted of treason and not pardoned`
    OR  `the person`'s `holds a temporary visa or is an unlawful noncitizen`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `barred from voting by section 18(1)` IF
        `barred from enrolment by section 18(2)` `the person`
    OR  `the person`'s `is serving or yet to serve 1 year or longer`

§§ `17 -- who is entitled to be enrolled and vote`

-- s 17(1): "Subject to the provisions of this Act, any person -- (a) who is -- (i) an Australian citizen; or (ii)" a non-citizen who
-- would be a British subject and was an elector "at some time within 3 months, immediately preceding 26 January 1984"; "and (b) who
-- has attained 18 years of age; and (c) who has lived in the same district for at least 1 month immediately before the enrolment, is
-- entitled -- (d) to be enrolled; and (e) when so enrolled and while continuing to live in that district, to vote in -- (i) any
-- Council election; and (ii) any election in the district."
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `meets section 17(1)(a)` IF
        `the person`'s `is an Australian citizen`
    OR  `the person`'s `is a pre-1984 British subject elector`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to be enrolled` IF
        `meets section 17(1)(a)` `the person`
    AND `the age` AT LEAST 18
    AND `the person`'s `has lived in the district for at least 1 month`
    AND (NOT `barred from enrolment by section 18(2)` `the person`)

-- s 4: "elector means a person who is enrolled". s 17AA(2): until a person enrolled under s 17AA(1) attains 18, the person "(a) is
-- taken not to be an elector; and (b) is not entitled to vote in an election".
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an elector` IF
        `the person`'s `is enrolled`
    AND `the age` AT LEAST 18

-- s 17(1)(e) with s 18(1). "election means a Council election or an election in a district" (s 4).
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age on polling day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to vote` IF
        `is an elector` `the person` `the age on polling day`
    AND `meets section 17(1)(a)` `the person`
    AND `the person`'s `continues to live in the district`
    AND (NOT `barred from voting by section 18(1)` `the person`)

-- s 17(2), (3): a person who fulfils s 17(1)(a) and (b), has lived in a district for at least 1 month ending immediately before the
-- day on which they intend to vote, and on that day is not enrolled (or not for that district) and "presents at a place to vote", is
-- entitled to be enrolled and, "if the person makes a claim for enrolment", "entitled to vote in the election on the relevant day as a
-- provisional voter under section 97G". (Subject to ss 145(7) and 172(1)(c), on new elections after a void one: not encoded.) That
-- s 18 still applies is an INFERENCE from "Subject to the provisions of this Act" in s 17(1) and the words of s 18(1).
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age on polling day` IS A NUMBER, `presents at a place to vote and claims enrolment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may vote as a provisional voter after enrolling on the day` IF
        `meets section 17(1)(a)` `the person`
    AND `the age on polling day` AT LEAST 18
    AND `the person`'s `has lived in the district for at least 1 month`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `is enrolled`)
    AND `presents at a place to vote and claims enrolment`
    AND (NOT `barred from voting by section 18(1)` `the person`)

§§ `17AA -- enrolment at 16 and 17`

-- s 17AA(1): "A person is entitled to be enrolled for a district if -- (a) the person has attained 16 years of age but has not attained
-- 18 years of age ...; and (b) the person would be entitled to be enrolled for the district if the person had attained 18 years of
-- age." (2): until 18 the person is taken not to be an elector, is not entitled to vote, and "is taken to be a silent elector".
-- Inserted by No. 30 of 2023 s 16 (in operation 1 July 2024, per the compilation table): it was not law on 13 March 2021. The s 17AA(3)
-- case (a person who does not know their age) is not encoded.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to be enrolled at 16 or 17` IF
        `the age` AT LEAST 16
    AND `the age` LESS THAN 18
    AND `entitled to be enrolled` `the person` 18

§§ `156(1), (16) -- the duty to vote and the offence`

-- s 156(1): "An elector must vote in any election for the whole of State electorate, and in any election for the district for which
-- the elector is enrolled, unless prevented from doing so by absence from the State, or because the person has a mental or physical
-- impairment on the days on which voting occurs in the election." s 16C(1): the State is a single electorate, the whole of State
-- electorate, for the election of members of the Council.
-- The duty is laid on "an elector", not on a person entitled to vote: read literally it reaches an enrolled prisoner whom s 18(1)(c)
-- bars from voting. That s 156(5)(c) ("was ineligible to vote") answers him is the only relief the section gives.
DECLARE Polling HAS
    `voted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was absent from the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had a mental or physical impairment on the voting days` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is dead` IS A BOOLEAN
    `believes abstaining is a religious duty` IS A BOOLEAN
    `had another valid and sufficient reason` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age on polling day` IS A NUMBER, `the polling` IS A Polling
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must vote` IF
        `is an elector` `the person` `the age on polling day`
    AND (NOT `the polling`'s `was absent from the State`)
    AND (NOT `the polling`'s `had a mental or physical impairment on the voting days`)

-- s 156(1A): "a valid and sufficient reason in relation to a failure to vote includes an honest belief on the part of an elector that
-- abstaining from voting is part of their religious duty". Otherwise the Act does not define it: an INPUT.
GIVEN `the polling` IS A Polling
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a valid and sufficient reason` IF
        `the polling`'s `believes abstaining is a religious duty`
    OR  `the polling`'s `had another valid and sufficient reason`

-- s 156(16): "If an elector fails to vote in an election without a valid and sufficient reason, the elector commits an offence.
-- Penalty for this subsection: a fine of $200." Reading the offence as requiring the s 156(1) duty (so that absence from the State
-- or impairment is an answer even if not called a reason) is an INFERENCE.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age on polling day` IS A NUMBER, `the polling` IS A Polling
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `commits the offence of failing to vote` IF
        `must vote` `the person` `the age on polling day` `the polling`
    AND (NOT `the polling`'s `voted`)
    AND (NOT `has a valid and sufficient reason` `the polling`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fine for failing to vote` MEANS 200

-- s 156(16A): a statement in response to a penalty or infringement notice "that the elector knows to be false or misleading in a
-- material particular": "a fine of $1 000".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the fine for a false response` MEANS 1000

§§ `156(2)-(8) -- the non-voters' list and the penalty notice`

-- s 156(2): the Commissioner must prepare a list of "the electors who were on the roll ... and did not vote". (4): "within the
-- prescribed period after the close of each election, the Electoral Commissioner shall send a penalty notice to each elector whose
-- name appears on the list" -- subject to (5): the Commissioner "does not have to send a penalty notice to an elector if ... satisfied
-- that the elector -- (a) is dead; or (b) was outside the State on polling day; or (c) was ineligible to vote in the election; or (d)
-- had a valid and sufficient reason for failing to vote". The prescribed period is not in the Act: not encoded.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age on polling day` IS A NUMBER, `the polling` IS A Polling
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is on the non-voters list` IF
        `is an elector` `the person` `the age on polling day`
    AND (NOT `the polling`'s `voted`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age on polling day` IS A NUMBER, `the polling` IS A Polling
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may decline to send a penalty notice` IF
        `is on the non-voters list` `the person` `the age on polling day` `the polling`
    AND (    `the polling`'s `is dead`
         OR  `the polling`'s `was absent from the State`
         OR  (NOT `entitled to vote` `the person` `the age on polling day`)
         OR  `has a valid and sufficient reason` `the polling`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person, `the age on polling day` IS A NUMBER, `the polling` IS A Polling
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a penalty notice must be sent` IF
        `is on the non-voters list` `the person` `the age on polling day` `the polling`
    AND (NOT `the Commissioner may decline to send a penalty notice` `the person` `the age on polling day` `the polling`)

-- s 156(7): "The response date set out in a penalty notice shall not be less than 21 days after the day on which the notice is sent."
-- (13): the same for an infringement notice.
GIVEN `days from sending to the response date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the response date is lawful` IF
    `days from sending to the response date` AT LEAST 21

-- s 156(8): "The modified penalty set out in a penalty notice must be an amount not exceeding -- (a) if the elector has not previously
-- paid a modified penalty under this section or been convicted of an offence against this section -- $50; or (b) otherwise -- $75."
-- (13): the same caps for an infringement notice. A penalty paid under the Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 s 245 is not "under this
-- section". The amount actually set, up to the cap, is the Commissioner's: an INPUT.
GIVEN `has previously paid or been convicted under section 156` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum modified penalty` MEANS
    IF `has previously paid or been convicted under section 156` THEN 75 ELSE 50

§§ `156(11)-(15A) -- responding, the infringement notice, and removal from the register`

-- s 156(6)(c): the elector may, by the response date, (i) give particulars of having voted, (ii) give a valid and sufficient reason,
-- or (iii) pay the modified penalty. (11): if the Commissioner is satisfied on (i) or (ii), or the elector pays, "proceedings are not
-- to be taken against the elector for a contravention of subsection (16)".
DECLARE Response IS ONE OF
    `no response`
    `particulars of voting that satisfy the Commissioner`
    `particulars of voting that do not satisfy the Commissioner`
    `a reason that satisfies the Commissioner`
    `a reason that does not satisfy the Commissioner`
    `payment of the modified penalty`

GIVEN `the response` IS A Response
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the penalty notice bars proceedings` IF
    CONSIDER `the response`
    WHEN `particulars of voting that satisfy the Commissioner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a reason that satisfies the Commissioner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `payment of the modified penalty` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 156(12), (13A): if the elector does not respond by the response date, or responds under (6)(c)(i) or (ii) and the Commissioner is
-- not satisfied, the Commissioner "may send to the elector an infringement notice" offering a modified penalty instead of prosecution.
-- (14): paying it by its response date means "proceedings are not to be taken against the elector for a contravention of subsection
-- (16)(a)". The subsection cited, (16)(a), does not exist in this compilation: s 156(16) has no paragraphs. Read as (16) here.
GIVEN `the response` IS A Response
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an infringement notice may be sent` IF
    NOT `the penalty notice bars proceedings` `the response`

GIVEN `the response` IS A Response, `paid the infringement notice penalty in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings for failing to vote are barred` IF
        `the penalty notice bars proceedings` `the response`
    OR  (`an infringement notice may be sent` `the response` AND `paid the infringement notice penalty in time`)

-- s 156(15): at the conclusion of an election the Commissioner must find out whether a person who "failed or neglected to respond to a
-- penalty notice or an infringement notice" still lives at the roll address, and if satisfied they do not, "cause the name of that
-- person to be removed from the register of electors". (15A): they must make a new claim before being reinstated.
GIVEN `failed to respond to a notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `still lives at the roll address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the name must be removed from the register` IF
        `failed to respond to a notice`
    AND (NOT `still lives at the roll address`)
